 "title": "Sales techniques to learn from doctors",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator claims that the best salesmen are doctors because of how they treat patients. He explains 5 key points on how salespeople should approach customers just like a doctor approaches a patient, focusing on diagnosing problems and building trust rather than just pushing products.",
 "key_points": [
  "Point 1: Listen before speaking. A doctor first asks about the problem and examines the patient before prescribing medicine, unlike a salesperson who praises their product before the customer even speaks.",
  "Point 2: Sell the solution, not the product. A doctor focuses on the right treatment for the patient's problem, so a salesperson should focus on how their product solves the customer's problem.",
  "Point 3: Do not offer discounts to gain trust. Offering discounts every time a customer asks devalues your product. Instead, prove your value and solution first.",
  "Point 4: Trust is your real marketing. When a doctor gives good treatment, patients recommend them to others, leading to word-of-mouth marketing and new customers.",
  "Point 5: Your personality is your brand. A doctor's advice, speech, clinic environment, and overall experience create their reputation, just like how your product, service, and customer experience build your brand.",
  "Summary quote: Don't just sell a product, diagnose the problem, prescribe the solution, and earn the trust."
